// # oodar — Gen 1 Host Substrate (v1.0.0)
//
// Logline: The canonical home of the openOODA Gen 1 host substrate. Compiled openOODA binaries link against the oo_* symbols exported from the 17 per-domain subdirs; the build entry point is `gcc oodar.c`.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. The C sources are organized into 17 per-domain subdirs, each with its own ANCHOR.oo describing the contents. The umbrella oodar.c is the single-TU build entry — it #include's the 46 .c files in dependency order. The public API is oodar.h Per-subdir headers live next to the .c files that own them.
//
// Beats (read in this order):
//   1. types.h          — shared type defs (OoStr, OoIList, OoRes*, OoLL*, OoControlBlock, OoWeakRef, ...).
//   2. oodar.h          — the public API surface (renamed in v1.0.0 from the historical name).
//   3. oodar.c          — the umbrella TU (the canonical single-TU build entry).
//   4. cap/             — the 14 unforgeable capability tokens (Pillar 5). Includes oodar_cap_init/drop/is_sandboxed/apply_seccomp_filter.
//   5. landlock/        — kernel-mediated FS containment (Pillar 9) + live-RAM proc_mem reader.
//   6. mem/             — linear arena + ARC + 64-byte aligned payload.
//   7. crypto/          — symmetric + AEAD + hash (constant-time primitives).
//   8. pqc/             — post-quantum (mlkem-768, mldsa-65). PQC-by-default in every emitted .oo program.
//   9. os/              — OS surface (sys_exec, sys_args, FS, DNS loopback-only, rlimit, time+rand).
//  10. net/             — network primitives (URL fetch, TLS client). Bound to os/netfloor loopback constraint.
//  11. io/              — print family.
//  12. actor/           — OTP-style actors + channels + joinable pthread threads + closures + cycle detection.
//  13. gpu/             — HIP/ROCm + compute kernels. No CPU fallback (fail-closed).
//  14. xlang/           — FFI (cap-gated, signature-verified) + xlang dispatch.
//  15. str/             — OoStr + interning + ops. str/str_from_int.c is the integer interning (the "str_int"→"str_from_int" rename drops the int=internal naming clash too).
//  16. list/            — OoIList / OoSList / OoFList / nested lists (X-macro compressed).
//  17. telemetry/       — metrics + event bus (decoupled from crypto via named events).
//  18. math/ meta/ hitl/ — math primitives, meta-circular primitives, human-in-the-loop.
//
// Naming convention:
//   - Files: <subdir>/<thing>.c  (no file prefix; one concept per file)
//   - Headers: oodar.h (root, public), types.h (root, shared), per-subdir <thing>.h
//   - Symbols: oo_* (the openOODA namespace; language-agnostic, project-namespaced)
//   - Subdir ANCHOR.oo: each subdir documents its own files and reading order
//
// Build:
//   gcc oodar.c                           (the canonical single-TU build)
//   gcc -c <subdir>/<file>.c             (per-file compile, link all .o)
//   gcc oodar.c <subdir>/<file>.c ...      (mix umbrella + per-file .o as needed)
//
// Versioning:
//   v1.0.0 is a Floor break from v0.1.x per RULES.oot §1.21. See VERSION.
//   Per RULES.oot §1.24 + RFC-0006, every push to main triggers an
//   auto-release via the governance workflow.
//
// residual: dudect_c_native.c (pqc/) and oo_hip_so_smoke.c (gpu/) move to qa/ in a follow-up.
// residual: cap-gate the weak-ref mutators (mem/weak.c) — Floor break, planned for v2.0.0.
//
// ──▓▓ oodar ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: api_surface = 53 :: VERSION = 1.0.0 :: Pillar 5 + Pillar 7 + Pillar 9 ::
